steps.prompt_template:
Call `check_plan` with `tools`: every tool the plan below uses, exactly as the plan writes it — each tool step's tool, each new agent's tools, and each tool under "Asks you first" and "Acts without asking", however the plan phrases it. Tools only: never a step, an agent, a state key or an output. With none, call it with {"tools": []}. It checks every tool and agent the plan names (F492, F666).

The plan:
{state.plan_draft}

Call `prepare_connection` for what the person wants connected:
{state.user_message}

Pick the kind: an app from this workspace's catalogue (`app`, by `catalog_slug`), a remote MCP server (`mcp_server`, an https `url`), a model provider's key (`provider_key`, by `provider`: openai, anthropic, gemini…), a custom tool's secret header (`tool_secret`), or a settings screen (`settings`, by `screen`). Give it a short `title` and one-sentence `why`.

Workspace profile (what this organisation does — read this first, it decides what a good answer looks like):
{state.org_profile}

Intent (already decided upstream): {state.intent}

User message: {state.user_message}

Chat history:
{state.chat_history}

Pre-selected agent IDs: {state.selected_agent_ids}
Can create new agents: {state.can_create_agents}
{state.knowledge_steps}{state.export_guide}
Current orchestration ID (may be empty): {state.current_orchestration_id}

Existing orchestration JSON (only populated on update):
{state.existing_orch}

Latest user clarification (empty on first pass):
{state.human_response}

Produce EITHER a complete requirements spec (prose, structured per your system prompt) OR one sharp clarifying question. Write it as your final response — it will be stored in the `requirements` state key, and a downstream evaluator decides whether to route to the planner or back to the user.

